              "lines": [
                "<span style=\"text-align:center;display:block;\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;font-weight: 700;\">IoT Sensor Fleet Monitoring — Real-Time Temperature & Humidity</span></span>\n",
                "\n",
                "<span style=\"text-align:center;display:block;\">Live-updating pipeline built with Databricks Auto Loader-style ingestion and streaming tables, tracking 10 simulated IoT sensors. Data is cleaned and watermarked to handle late-arriving readings, then aggregated into 5-minute rolling windows per device. Most devices hold steady in the 25-30°C / 40-55% humidity range, with occasional short-lived swings (e.g. device\\_2 dipping to \\~20°C before recovering) — the kind of anomaly a real monitoring system would flag for investigation.</span>"
              ]
